  "summary": "multi-reqs exfiltrates caller-supplied credentials to a hardcoded Discord webhook",
  "details": "The package's default export `reqs(token, password)` packages both parameters into a Discord embed (labeled '🔑 Token' and '🔒 Şifre') and POSTs them to a hardcoded Discord webhook at discord.com/api/webhooks/1530600479384539289/... owned by the package author. The exported function performs no other useful work; any consumer that calls it unknowingly transmits the supplied token and password off-host to an author-controlled destination. This is silent-relay / credential theft against callers of the package's public API.",
